mockcomp -- a scriptable Wayland compositor for testing the native
Wayland backend.

Build and check it inside `nix develop':

  make -C test/wayland/mockcomp
  make -C test/wayland/mockcomp check

Run it:

  mockcomp --socket NAME --control PATH [--trace FILE] [--snapshots DIRECTORY]

It listens on the Wayland socket NAME in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, prints
"mockcomp ready ..." on stdout when clients may connect, writes every
request and event to the trace FILE, and accepts commands on the Unix
socket PATH.  Its exit status is 2 if it recorded any protocol
invariant violation.

`--snapshots` writes the attached shm image on each content commit.
The rendering runner gives each captured client its own mockcomp
instance and snapshot directory. Mockcomp and Emacs's
`wayland--dump-frame` name each PNG by surface ID and content commit.

Globals: wl_compositor 6, wl_shm, wl_seat 8 (keyboard with a "us"
keymap, pointer; --seat-version gives an older version, which tests
the axis events of older seats), wl_output 4, wl_data_device_manager
3, xdg_wm_base 6, zxdg_output_manager_v1 3, wp_cursor_shape_manager_v1
1 (withheld by --no-cursor-shape), and, unless a fixture removes them,
wp_viewporter and wp_fractional_scale_manager_v1.  Status reports the
last cursor shape, how many shapes and wl_pointer.set_cursor requests
arrived, and whether the last set_cursor hid the pointer.

Outputs: MOCK-1 is 1920x1080 at scale 1.  MOCK-2, added by `output
add', is 1920x1080 at 150%: wl_output.scale reports 2, as compositors
round fractional scales up, and only xdg-output gives its exact
logical size, 1280x720 at x=1920.

Invariant checks, each recorded as a violation:

  attach-before-configure   buffer on an xdg surface's initial commit
                            (also a protocol error, as compositors do)
  commit-before-ack         buffer committed before any configure ack
  invalid-ack-serial        ack of an unsent or already-acked serial
  reuse-of-held-buffer      attaching a buffer mockcomp still holds,
                            other than the current one
  damage-outside-buffer     damage_buffer beyond the buffer's size
  xdg-surface-with-buffer   xdg surface created for a surface with a
                            buffer
  unexpected-popup          the backend has no popups

Control commands, one per line; each gets one reply line ("ok",
"error ...", or JSON):

  status                    counters and violations, as JSON, with
                            the held buffers and their sizes; with a
                            mapped surface, also its last buffer size
                            and whether its latest configure is acked
  ping                      xdg_wm_base.ping to every client
  key KEYCODE press|release evdev key event to the focused surface,
                            focusing the first mapped surface if none
                            is; modifiers follow from mockcomp's own
                            xkb state and are sent when they change
  focus SURFACE|none        move keyboard focus (leave, then enter and
                            modifiers)
  repeat-info RATE DELAY    send wl_keyboard.repeat_info (rate 0
                            disables repeat)
  layout LAYOUT[:VARIANT]   compile and send a new keymap, e.g. de or
                            us:intl for dead keys
  pointer enter SURFACE X Y | motion X Y | leave
                            pointer focus and motion, in logical
                            surface coordinates
  pointer button CODE press|release
                            evdev button, e.g. 272 for BTN_LEFT
  pointer axis vertical|horizontal VALUE wheel|finger|continuous
                            [VALUE120]
                            an axis event with its source; VALUE120 is
                            sent as axis_value120, or as axis_discrete
                            below wl_seat 8
  pointer stop vertical|horizontal
                            axis_stop, which ends finger scrolling
  clock real|MS             timestamps from the real clock, or from a
                            manual clock set to MS
  im preedit BEGIN END TEXT | im commit TEXT | im delete BEFORE AFTER
  | im done [SERIAL]
                            text-input-v3 events to the focused client;
                            done's serial defaults to the object's
                            commit count.  Text inputs get enter and
                            leave as keyboard focus moves, and status
                            reports the newest one under "im"
  offer-selection TEXT      offer TEXT as the selection
                            (text/plain;charset=utf-8)
  request-selection         request the registered M0 test source on a pipe
  selection-result          pending until the writer closes, then ok only
                            if the fixed test payload arrived intact
  stall on|off              stop or resume reading client requests;
                            events from commands are still sent
  hold-buffers on|off       keep or release superseded buffers
  frame-callbacks on|off    fire frame callbacks every 16 ms, or not
  configure W H [W H]...    send each size as a toplevel configure to
                            every configured toplevel, as one burst
                            (0 leaves that axis to the client)
  protocol-error            post an error on the first xdg_wm_base
  protocol-error-epipe      send that error and reject the next client write
  disconnect-on-commit      drop the client at the next content commit
  disconnect                drop every client
  quit                      exit

Planned fixtures: the damage-only image, out-of-order releases,
configure states, output hotplug, the
input-method role, and a deterministic clock.
